From: Zmax Ntrust maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] fs/locks: account file lock caches to their memory cgroup
SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only

Restore the accounting from upstream commit
0f12156dff2862ac54235fc72703f18770769042 (Vasily Averin), reviewed by
Shakeel Butt and merged by Linus Torvalds. It was reverted by
3754707bcc3e190e5dadc978d172b61e809cb3bd for a file-lock microbenchmark
regression, not a correctness defect. This appliance chooses enforceable
service memory limits over that microbenchmark performance.

Adapt the flags to Linux 7.2.10, including the subsequently separated lease
cache. No new allocation, locking or concurrency implementation is added.

CVE: CVE-2022-0480
Upstream: https://github.com/torvalds/linux/commit/0f12156dff2862ac54235fc72703f18770769042
Revert: https://github.com/torvalds/linux/commit/3754707bcc3e190e5dadc978d172b61e809cb3bd

--- a/fs/locks.c
+++ b/fs/locks.c
@@ -3142,13 +3142,16 @@
 	int i;
 
 	flctx_cache = kmem_cache_create("file_lock_ctx",
-			sizeof(struct file_lock_context), 0, SLAB_PANIC, NULL);
+			sizeof(struct file_lock_context), 0,
+			SLAB_PANIC | SLAB_ACCOUNT, NULL);
 
 	filelock_cache = kmem_cache_create("file_lock_cache",
-			sizeof(struct file_lock), 0, SLAB_PANIC, NULL);
+			sizeof(struct file_lock), 0,
+			SLAB_PANIC | SLAB_ACCOUNT, NULL);
 
 	filelease_cache = kmem_cache_create("file_lease_cache",
-			sizeof(struct file_lease), 0, SLAB_PANIC, NULL);
+			sizeof(struct file_lease), 0,
+			SLAB_PANIC | SLAB_ACCOUNT, NULL);
 
 	for_each_possible_cpu(i) {
 		struct file_lock_list_struct *fll = per_cpu_ptr(&file_lock_list, i);
